redfin 1225: Touch ID failed-match lockout as on iOS, kern.sweet_mesa_lockout (default 0 = old behaviour)

BiometricKit maps the 39 GetSKSLockState bits to the lockout state (BKDevice lockoutState:fromDeviceLockoutState:)
and biometrickitd asks 39 after every no-match record (getBioLockoutState, the match result's LockoutState).
SpringBoard (_SBUIBiometricKitInterface matchedWithResult:) turns a no-identity result with state 4 into event 11
"match failed caused lockout" + event 6 (bio lockout: passcode required). The old answer (0x8 or 0) made every
refusal look like state 5 "expired" and the 5th failure was never reported as a lockout.
bit 0: 39 answers reason bits (0x8 allowed, 0x10 no passcode since boot, 0x4 five failures / forced, 0x2 backoff,
0 after 48 h). bit 1: failures count in every match mode. bit 2: 73 ForceBioLockout / 57 DropUnlockToken lock
Touch ID out until a passcode unlock (both logged). bit 3: 0xe3ff800a v1 {u32 user, u16 bits} when the answer
changes (lockout, keybag events). A passcode unlock already resets the count (1198); a Touch ID unlock resets it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013SvAC4dCbJuYfzxCtCk4D8
